0/10\u230b = 800\n- |A15| = \u230a8000/15\u230b = 533\n- All pairwise LCMs = 30 \u2192 each = \u230a8000/30\u230b = 266\n- Triple LCM = 30 \u2192 266\n\n|S| = 1333+800+533 \u2212 266\u2212266\u2212266 + 266 = 2666 \u2212 798 + 266 = **2134**\n\n**Step 2: Count of those also divisible by 17 (subtract these)**\n\nNeed count divisible by 17 AND (6 or 10 or 15) \u2014 i.e., divisible by 102, 170, or 255.\n\n- \u230a8000/102\u230b = 78\n- \u230a8000/170\u230b = 47\n- \u230a8000/255\u230b = 31\n- lcm(102,170)=lcm(102,255)=lcm(170,255)=510 \u2192 \u230a8000/510\u230b = 15 (each pair)\n- Triple lcm = 510 \u2192 15\n\n|B| = 78+47+31 \u2212 15\u221215\u221215 + 15 = 156 \u2212 45 + 15 = **126**\n\n**Step 3: Final count**\n\n2134 \u2212 126 = **2008**\n\nFINAL: 1029.72; 1113; 2008"
